cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dy-wcet: worst-case response time in integer arithmetic"
message: "If you use this software in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Yermakou"
    given-names: "Denis"
    email: "connect@axonos.org"
    affiliation: "DY Research"
abstract: >-
  Response-time analysis for fixed-priority task sets, computed entirely in
  integer arithmetic. Non-convergence returns an explicit unschedulable result
  rather than a capped value, and every operation is checked so that overflow
  cannot turn an unschedulable set into a schedulable-looking one.
repository-code: "https://github.com/DYResearch/dy-wcet"
version: "0.1.1"
date-released: "2026-08-17"
license: "Apache-2.0 OR MIT"
keywords:
  - real-time systems
  - response-time analysis
  - fixed-priority scheduling
  - embedded


